com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.7.2.stable.mono.official [ed1daf0bf]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.2.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9649) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhere Body A's layer overlaps Body B's mask, but Body B does not share a layer with Body A, Body A will intermittently and strangely react to Body B if Body A has Continuous CD enabled.\n\nThe expected behaviour would be that Body A does not respond to Body B, and Body B responds as if Body A had infinite mass.\n\nThis bug is only present in Jolt 3D physics, Godot Physics seems fine.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nEnsure Jolt 3d Physics is enabled.\n\nCreate Body A and enable CD\nCreate Body B and set it so it shares a mask layer with Body As collision layer, but does not share a collision layer. Easily done by just disabling all collision layers of Body B.\n\nCause a CD collision (some velocity on Body A is required).\n\nBody A _will_ respond to Body B, getting stuck inside it and sluggishly moving until the collision ends.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nIn this project, there are two near-identical collisions: an object falls onto another, where the top object has a collision layer + mask but the bottom object only has a mask.\n\nThe difference is the left falling object has Continuous CD enabled and the right does not. The left falling object will sluggishly sink to the floor once the collision starts, whereas the right falling object with no CCD will push the other object out of the way as if it had infinite mass.\n\n[continous-cd-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31921352/continous-cd-bug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123281/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}